          "Structure_Text": {
            "original": "The as-printed alloy has a conventional polycrystalline morphology with an average grain size of 29.7 μm and an average KAM value of 0.85°. Cellular structures with an average size of ~400 nm prevail inside the grains. The cellular walls were decorated with a high density of dislocations, with relatively few dislocations inside. SADP verifies the single-phase FCC structure without any superlattice spots. The cellular walls are obviously enriched in Ti and slightly depleted in Co and Cr. Ni and Al show no significant partitioning behavior at the cellular walls.",
